{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-32270",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t) & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 1}({t}^{2}),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 1}({t}^{3}),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 1}(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{1}^{2},{1}^{3},\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}g(t) & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 1}(5-{t}^{3}),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 1}({t}^{2}-t+2),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 1}(4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5-{1}^{3},{1}^{2}-1+2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,2,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}[5f(t)+2g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 1}5f(t)+{lim}_{t\\to 1}2g(t) \\\\  & =5{lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t)+2{lim}_{t\\to 1}g(t) \\\\  & =5⟨1,1,1⟩+2⟨4,2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,5,5⟩+⟨8,4,8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨13,9,13⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
